Entries for the New Hampshire QSO Party used by in-state (New Hampshire) stations
The 10 New Hampshire counties (each its own multiplier), the states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier (at most 10 in the score), not entries here.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before S50.DOM: the rules count "each state" and are silent on DC (an open question on issue 112).
NH itself is listed by S50.DOM but is no multiplier: the class refuses it (New Hampshire stations send their county).
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE newhampshire_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
